   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Connectors",
   "texto": [
    "**Lorsque** (when), **pendant que** (while), **depuis que** (since), **tandis que** (while, in contrast).",
    "Example: **Lorsque tu es là, nous mangeons** (when you are here, we eat)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Training and use",
   "texto": [
    "The **futur antérieur** is formed with **avoir** or **être** in future + past participle: **tu auras fini**.",
    "With **être**, the participle matches the subject: **elle sera arrivée**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Tell that and the future",
   "texto": [
    "**Dès que** (as soon as) introduces an action that can occur just before another.",
    "For two future actions, use a future time; if the first one will be completed before the second, use **futur antérieur**: **Dès que tu auras fini, je viendrai** (as soon as you finish, I will come)."
   ]
